Phase 8B: Consolidate physical storage into a configurable texture array
  Depends on Phase 8A. This approved storage decision supersedes earlier incremental bank-growth/shrink
  requirements and separate-texture bindings. Preserve the completed geometry, deformation, clipping and
  candidate work wherever its contracts remain applicable.
  Outcome: allocate one R32UI 2D texture array at configured capacity, with multiple physical page tiles
  per layer. Page occupancy changes within that allocation; demand does not grow or shrink the resource.
  Explicit capacity/layout configuration changes recreate the pool and invalidate its cached pages.

  Controlling sources: [proposal: sampling, allocation and lifecycle](Rendering.VirtualShadowMaps.Proposal.md#sampling-allocation-and-lifecycle-contract),
  [proposal: integer tiles](Rendering.VirtualShadowMaps.Proposal.md#integer-tiles-clearing-and-sampling),
  [contracts: physical pages and sampling](Rendering.VirtualShadowMaps.Contracts.md#projections-physical-pages-and-sampling),
  [contracts: settings and effective policy](Rendering.VirtualShadowMaps.Contracts.md#persisted-settings-and-effective-policy),
  and [qualification: evidence routes and correctness matrix](Rendering.VirtualShadowMaps.Qualification.md).
  These sources govern every subtask below; retained temporal, ownership and failure contracts apply unchanged.

  Completion, 2026-11-11: second source review, configured independent test review and independent
  completion audit passed with no unresolved findings. Evidence paths are relative to this document:
    [Strict Debug/content build](../artifacts/virtual-shadow-maps/texture-array-pool/20261111-215323/strict-debug.log)
    passed with 21 warnings and zero errors. [Warning classification](../artifacts/virtual-shadow-maps/texture-array-pool/20261111-215323/build-warning-classification.json)
    attributes these warnings to unchanged source or existing generated owners.
